       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A dose of 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visits, isn't a clinical reason for exceeding that limit. The risk is serious: lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity can happen even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter either of these now:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **A lower dose or titration schedule**, such as 500 mg or 850 mg twice daily, increased as tolerated\n\nIf you have a clinical reason for going above the labeled maximum, you can enter the order directly. Pharmacy will then review it. I'd also suggest talking to the pharmacist first.\n\nIf you want the order to include a note, such as \"discussed with family, titration planned,\" I can add that. Which option would you like?"
